A||N||5||Lewis||Idle problem poor gas mileage and ticking sound||||9||
Z||000000||Lewis||03-16-2000||10:00 AM||||I have a 85GT,auto and when my car warms up the idle goes down to about 600/700 and then dies. Does not do this all the time but enough to be a pain in the butt. Also I noticed that the exhaust is very strong and the car burns a lot of gas. Also have a ticking sound that is coming from the engine. Seems to be near the engine that is closest to the back window could it be the exhaust manifold?||||reg||9
Z||000001||mshill||03-16-2000||12:42 PM||||Lewis,  that ticking sound from the firewall side of the engine is most likely a cracked manifold.  This is also likely to be a source of poor gas mileage.  Someone else will have to comment on the low idle/stall issure since I have a manual V6 and never had a problem with low idle.||||reg||13
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||03-17-2000||01:00 AM||||   Lewis, The idle problem could be your IAC valve(IDLE AIR CONTROL). I had similar symptoms and that was the cure. Also, you might experience Idle surge or hunting. This is where the idle speed fluxuates. If you are experiencing this, more than likely it's your IAC. As for the gas milage issue try a basic tune-up ie...plugs, wires, cap and rotor, do not omit the plug wires. also check<BR>your EGR. I had EGR problems; when I replaced my EGR tube and Vacuum regualtor(it<BR>was kind of pricey) my gas milage increased.<BR>The ticking noise "could" be a cracked manifold, but it "could" also be a bad lifter. Hopefully you know someone who can tell the difference. Let us know what you find out. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> BAM OUT!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||12
Z||000003||Shiner||03-17-2000||01:21 AM||||Lewis,<P> When you have a cracked manifold, the ticking will get louded when the engine is under a heavy load.  My '87 GT's front manifold is cracked, but you can't hear it at idle or when you are cruising, just when you give it a good shot of throttle.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WisconsinGT||03-17-2000||09:06 AM||||It does not have to e a cracked manafold. I just fixed an exhaust leak that had the same symtems you are having. It turned out that the connection between the firewall exhaust manafold and the downpipe it connects to was loose. All is well now. Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Lewis||03-17-2000||09:37 AM||||Thanks for the relply's.  I will look into all the suggestions today.  I hope it is not anything expensive..not sure what the costs are for manifold or gasket.  Will also put car on the hoist and check for loose connections and cracks..and will give it a tune up...and retrieve any codes..lewis||||reg||14
